(7638561, 1239741, 67258, '<td valign="top">I''ve revisited this a couple of times, and am bumping to a 9.  It has a real arty, illustration type feel to it - I can imagine it as a framed poster or print.<br/> <br/>Edit, back for another view - and another bump. That''s your lot :D</td>', 'I''ve revisited this a couple of times, and am bumping to a 9.  It has a real arty, illustration type feel to it - I can imagine it as a framed poster or print. Edit, back for another view - and another bump. That''s your lot :D', '2019-08-20 08:14:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7638562, 1239721, 67258, '<td valign="top">Whilst I like many ''arty'' photos, I am not usually fan of what I would describe as painting imitations, but I make an exception here.  The poses, the moment is so perfectly captured.  I find myself intrigued by the story - the slightly old fashioned dresses and shoes, the sashes, and similar hats - are the ladies dancers - or were they?  There is something very graceful about the pose of the more slender lady.  the wind catching the skirts adds the necessary movement to give the sense of a fleeting moment.<br/> <br/>I would be intrigued to see a version of the image edited in a more straightforward manner,  but I suspect that I would still like this one best.  I now have an interesting internal debate with myself about photography/art/painting....<br/> <br/>Bumping from 7 to 9.</td>', 'Whilst I like many ''arty'' photos, I am not usually fan of what I would describe as painting imitations, but I make an exception here.  The poses, the moment is so perfectly captured.  I find myself intrigued by the story - the slightly old fashioned dresses and shoes, the sashes, and similar hats - are the ladies dancers - or were they?  There is something very graceful about the pose of the more slender lady.  the wind catching the skirts adds the necessary movement to give the sense of a fleeting moment. I would be intrigued to see a version of the image edited in a more straightforward manner,  but I suspect that I would still like this one best.  I now have an interesting internal debate with myself about photography/art/painting.... Bumping from 7 to 9.', '2019-08-20 08:25:47.000000', NULL, 1),
