(7639176, 1239881, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by marnet:</b></div><hr/><i> Did you add the animal to the landscape? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No, it was there already:)<br/> <br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1240169" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/135744/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1240169.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/135744/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1240169.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/135744/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1240169.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Originally posted by marnet: Did you add the animal to the landscape?   No, it was there already:) ', '2019-08-23 05:16:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(7639244, 1239897, 144365, '<td valign="top"><i><b>Anyone want to tell me (brutal honesty is fine with me!) what''s wrong with my entry?</b></i> <br/>Lighting is a mess. The shrimp look like they were cut and put into this scene without regard of keeping continuity with the lighting of the surroundings; same with the flamingos. Shadows are missing. The flamingo standing on the plate should have a shadow that points to the lower left part of the image. You can see the shadow from the leg of the dresser cast by the window present in the scene. <br/> <br/>From your comments: <i>Then, I put them in the scene, but there was no "story".<br/>WHY were they there? </i> <br/>Even with the shrimp, there''s no story. It doesn''t make sense.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2019-08-23 14:27:06.</i></td>', 'Anyone want to tell me (brutal honesty is fine with me!) what''s wrong with my entry? Lighting is a mess. The shrimp look like they were cut and put into this scene without regard of keeping continuity with the lighting of the surroundings; same with the flamingos. Shadows are missing. The flamingo standing on the plate should have a shadow that points to the lower left part of the image. You can see the shadow from the leg of the dresser cast by the window present in the scene.  From your comments: Then, I put them in the scene, but there was no "story".WHY were they there?  Even with the shrimp, there''s no story. It doesn''t make sense.', '2019-08-23 15:11:22.000000', '2019-08-23 15:27:06.000000', 0),
(7639254, 1239897, 156466, '<td valign="top">Because you asked... I gave you a 6 for the work, but there''s a lot here. Venser has covered much of it, particularly around "story" (you might have been able to tie it in with a title if you built it around "pink") but I''ll add some. <br/> <br/>When you''re compositing you need to look at light and just looking at the coat rack you can see that light/shadows fan out from just that image and fade quickly, not like those on the flamingo that has them.<br/> <br/>From there you''ve utterly messed with my OCD when it comes to lines and while the floor is fine your verticals are a bit of a mess for me, and a corner line always wins to a coat rack. You''re shooting the room into the corner when perhaps you should have moved right and shot with the image plan parallel to the far wall.<br/> <br/>Finally, it''s vertical, and while I can see a lot of details here when it''s presented to vote in a squashed format you lose details and nuance. I stay away from verticals whenever possible here for that reason.</td>', 'Because you asked... I gave you a 6 for the work, but there''s a lot here. Venser has covered much of it, particularly around "story" (you might have been able to tie it in with a title if you built it around "pink") but I''ll add some.  When you''re compositing you need to look at light and just looking at the coat rack you can see that light/shadows fan out from just that image and fade quickly, not like those on the flamingo that has them. From there you''ve utterly messed with my OCD when it comes to lines and while the floor is fine your verticals are a bit of a mess for me, and a corner line always wins to a coat rack. You''re shooting the room into the corner when perhaps you should have moved right and shot with the image plan parallel to the far wall. Finally, it''s vertical, and while I can see a lot of details here when it''s presented to vote in a squashed format you lose details and nuance. I stay away from verticals whenever possible here for that reason.', '2019-08-23 16:46:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(7639273, 1239206, 80096, '<td valign="top">I think your peacock is stupendous! Detail/color is amazing and I enjoyed your attached story.. but no mention of the peacock''s cry. Once you get to know the cry it''s easy to identify where it came from. Some think it sounds like a cat but it''s very loud and can be heard from great distances.</td>', 'I think your peacock is stupendous! Detail/color is amazing and I enjoyed your attached story.. but no mention of the peacock''s cry. Once you get to know the cry it''s easy to identify where it came from. Some think it sounds like a cat but it''s very loud and can be heard from great distances.', '2019-08-23 21:46:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7639347, 1239206, 24454, '<td valign="top">What a great story!  Oh how I would love to have a resident bird like this in my very own yard!  You have some glorious birds in your neck of the woods!  I love this bright colorful art.  It makes me happy.</td>', 'What a great story!  Oh how I would love to have a resident bird like this in my very own yard!  You have some glorious birds in your neck of the woods!  I love this bright colorful art.  It makes me happy.', '2019-08-24 12:30:20.000000', NULL, 0),
